4,"o":"api_cash_load"},{"a":52341,"t":"code","b":[76,240,2],"m":"jmp","oa":752,"o":"api_print_long"},{"a":52344,"l":"doctor_text","c":"Module 0's packed text block (5-bit codes read from the lowest bit up; work/text.py decodes it), first its 60-byte alphabet, codes 0-$29: space e o (end) t n RETURN a s i r d l h y u p m w c . g (code 4) b ) $ \" (code 6) v : ' (code $0B, the name) x f ? = 7 6 1 , # (code 3); $2A-$3B hold $7F and are not used. Codes $1E (capital) and $1F (escape) are not letters, so the entries at $1E and $1F (' and code $0B) are reached as escape plus 0 and plus 1. doctor_print points $43/$44 here.","t":"byte","b":[32,101,111,0,116,110,13,97]},{"a":52352,"t":"byte","b":[115,105,114,100,108,104,121,117]},{"a":52360,"t":"byte","b":[112,109,119,99,46,103,4,98]},{"a":52368,"t":"byte","b":[41,36,34,6,118,58,39,11]},{"a":52376,"t":"byte","b":[120,102,63,61,55,54,49,44]},{"a":52384,"t":"byte","b":[35,3,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52392,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52400,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127]},{"a":52404,"l":"doctor_text_groups","c":"Seven offsets, each counted from this table at $CCB4, to the message groups of the doctor's text: $000E (group 0 at $CCC2), $002E ($CCE2), $0046 ($CCFA), $0077 ($CD2B), $00AA ($CD5E), $00FB ($CDAF), $0124 ($CDD8). Message n is in group n/4; find_message ($1E0E) decodes and drops the messages before it in its group.","t":"word","b":[14,0,46,0,70,0,119,0],"d":[14,46,70,119]},{"a":52412,"t":"word","b":[170,0,251,0,36,1],"d":[170,251,292]},{"a":52418,"l":"doctor_text_g0","c":"Message group 0 (messages 0-3, one bit stream): 0 empty, never printed; 1 \"Radiation poisoning\"; 2 \"Wasteland Herpes\"; 3 \"Bug byte\" (the names of the diseases in bits 0-2 of +$28, listed as 1-3).","t":"byte","b":[195,171,179,210,33,73,20,0]},{"a":52426,"t":"byte","b":[69,66,162,164,82,135,151,7]},{"a":52434,"t":"byte","b":[145,192,78,89,192,183,160,96]},{"a":52442,"t":"byte","b":[64,195,223,87,193,117,36,12]},{"a":52450,"l":"doctor_text_g1","c":"Message group 1 (messages 4-7): \"Sewer rot\", \"Desert dust\", \"Rabies\" and \"D6\", the names of the diseases in bits 3-6 of +$28 (D6 is a placeholder).","t":"byte","b":[30,5,25,20,80,130,12,191]},{"a":52458,"t":"byte","b":[2,10,138,128,245,16,25,94]},{"a":52466,"t":"byte","b":[157,155,2,26,126,253,51,0]},{"a":52474,"l":"doctor_text_g2","c":"Message group 2 (messages 8-11): 8 \"D7\", the placeholder name of bit 7; 9 RETURN, \"<name> is beyond my help.\", RETURN and code 6 (a (RETURN) wait); 10 code 4 (clear the window), two RETURNs, a quoted \"Well <name>, I would recommend:\" and RETURN; 11 \"E)xam $\".","t":"byte","b":[126,125,51,204,15,32,33,112]},{"a":52482,"t":"byte","b":[131,19,101,129,232,64,11,12]},{"a":52490,"t":"byte","b":[82,179,135,53,70,123,25,24]},{"a":52498,"t":"byte","b":[3,63,252,4,124,2,82,60]},{"a":52506,"t":"byte","b":[182,128,10,83,196,24,202,234]},{"a":52514,"t":"byte","b":[218,12,31,240,23,39,130,60]},{"a":52522,"t":"byte","b":[0]},{"a":52523,"l":"doctor_text_g3","c":"Message group 3 (messages 12-15): 12 RETURN, \"H)ealing\", RETURN; 13 RETURN, \"C)uring\"; 14 code 4, two RETURNs, \"Healing costs $\"; 15 \" per CON point.\", two RETURNs, \"You need to heal \".","t":"byte","b":[198,55,28,14,75,165,154,97]},{"a":52531,"t":"byte","b":[252,196,79,165,82,135,53,198]},{"a":52539,"t":"byte","b":[183,112,88,42,21,76,129,8]},{"a":52547,"t":"byte","b":[2,121,0,24,20,240,211,11]},{"a":52555,"t":"byte","b":[95,0,20,169,16,106,140,119]},{"a":52563,"t":"byte","b":[226,129,18,194,2,68,128,22]},{"a":52571,"t":"byte","b":[14,3,3]},{"a":52574,"l":"doctor_text_g4","c":"Message group 4 (messages 16-19): 16 \" points. Press Y to heal 1 point.\" and RETURN; 17 code 4, \"You have no diseases.\", RETURN, code 6; 18 code 4, \"You don't have enough money.\", RETURN, code 6; 19 code 4, a quoted \"You're inflicted with:\" and two RETURNs.","t":"byte","b":[0,138,84,8,162,192,67,21]},{"a":52582,"t":"byte","b":[16,2,222,1,34,64,11,135]},{"a":52590,"t":"byte","b":[129,143,0,20,169,16,106,134]},{"a":52598,"t":"byte","b":[245,78,60,208,14,15,160,8]},{"a":52606,"t":"byte","b":[176,18,10,7,5,68,205,30]},{"a":52614,"t":"byte","b":[214,59,241,192,18,229,3,2]},{"a":52622,"t":"byte","b":[218,225,1,132,34,94,109,32]},{"a":52630,"t":"byte","b":[138,18,28,53,123,88,237,157]},{"a":52638,"t":"byte","b":[120,31,168,0,82,249,131,165]},{"a":52646,"t":"byte","b":[73,194,2,50,145,214,181,49]},{"a":52654,"t":"byte","b":[3]},{"a":52655,"l":"doctor_text_g5","c":"Message group 5 (messages 20-23): 20 \"Enter # to cure at $\"; 21 \" each.\" and RETURN; 22 \"alot more\", printed instead of the number of points to heal when the patient is not conscious; 23 \"Who wants treatment?\" and RETURN.","t":"byte","b":[62,20,18,20,248,10,16,1]},{"a":52663,"t":"byte","b":[230,83,1,28,2,242,0,225]},{"a":52671,"t":"byte","b":[204,70,205,56,76,16,16,133]},{"a":52679,"t":"byte","b":[10,195,203,38,128,60,133,32]},{"a":52687,"t":"byte","b":[64,84,56,36,134,66,62,49]},{"a":52695,"t":"byte","b":[3]},{"a":52696,"l":"doctor_text_g6","c":"Message group 6, holding only message 24, the last: \"P)ool Money = $\" and code 3 (clear to the end of the line). Its end code finishes in bit 0 of $CDE5, the last byte of the block that is ever read. The byte after it, $CDE6 ($20), is the last value decoded from module 0's own packed bytes, from the stream's final four bits (code 1000, entry 0 of the value table); nothing reads it, and whether it was meant or is padding of the last byte is not known.","t":"byte","b":[30,98,33,24,240,81,148,224]},{"a":52704,"t":"byte","b":[192,47,32,255,53,0,32]},{"a":52711,"t":"gap","n":12825},{"a":52711,"t":"note","l":"doctor_unpack_overrun","c":"Not part of module 0, whose own bytes end at $CDE6. Its packed stream is 921 bytes, but the module directory gives the unpacker a window of four sectors (the entry's third byte), so it decodes on, with module 0's value table, into the stream that follows on the disk: module 1's on sides 1, 2 and 4 (on side 1 from track 25, logical sector 12, byte 153), module 2's on side 3, which is why side 3's copy differs from here on and ends at $CE5B. Nothing reads these bytes.","note":"outside the tracked image"}]}